WEBVTT

0
00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:08.020
Sprezzature is an AI engine for Design.
Ux-laws, the audit of the laws of UX.

1
00:00:08.219 --> 00:00:12.656
They will say the page is overwhelming
and they cannot find the button.

2
00:00:12.700 --> 00:00:16.980
Nobody will ever say HICK's Law.
Nobody knows its name.

3
00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:21.520
You get the symptom and never the cause,
published in 1952.

4
00:00:28.600 --> 00:00:32.240
30 laws, collected by Jon YABLONSKI.

5
00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:35.400
8 of them settle from the source alone.

6
00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:41.199
No browser, no rendering:
the median page takes 5 milliseconds.

7
00:00:41.600 --> 00:00:46.240
Fast enough to live in a pre-commit hook,
which is where a gate must live.

8
00:00:46.600 --> 00:00:50.287
HICK's Law counts the choices
a person meets at one moment.

9
00:00:52.600 --> 00:00:56.350
A responsive header holds 2
menus that never paint together.

10
00:00:57.400 --> 00:01:01.760
Adding them up charges the reader
for choices no screen ever shows.

11
00:01:03.600 --> 00:01:08.225
So the auditor places each control
and reports the worse count, naming it.

12
00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:13.840
A block that collapses is one choice,
whatever it holds.

13
00:01:17.800 --> 00:01:23.520
40 links in one nav, or 7.
One exits zero, the other exits one.

14
00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:29.080
40 is a fact about the markup.
Whether 40 is too many is not.

15
00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:35.440
It is a fast gate,
not a substitute for design review.

16
00:01:41.400 --> 00:01:46.360
Go to sprezzature.ai,
and drop a GitHub star if it deserves it.

17
00:01:49.600 --> 00:01:52.640
Make it, audit it, take a look at it.
